  "text": "Ford Motor Company is recalling 223,472 vehicles in the United States over an issue with the fuel tank that could result in a leak, the US National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) said on Saturday.\nThe recall will include certain n 2023-2027 F-150 vehicles. \"The fuel tank may be improperly secured and leak fuel, or detach from the vehicle while driving,\" the agency stated and added that a \"detached tank can create a road hazard, increasing the risk of a crash. In addition, a fuel leak can cause an engine stall or increase the risk of a fire.\"\nDealers will inspect the part and, if necessary, replace the fuel tank free of charge."
